# The Last Kingdom - a new island of the library, twenty times the size (x20)
# A whole small kingdom on one island, empty since its king died: the harbour town of Elderhaven on the north coast, a
# river through farmland with a watermill, a dark forest over the northern peak, a lake in the valley with a drowned
# chapel, and a castle on the southern peak's shoulder. The steward hid the crown in a vault under the castle court and
# scattered the three royal seals that open it; the Beast of Elderhaven sleeps in the great hall.
# Quest "The Crown of Elderhaven" (40 steps in 6 chapters): the town (the proclamation, the warehouse's rats, the reeve's
# writ, the market's hens, the innkeeper, the toll bridge), the farmlands (the mill's seal, the boars, the goats, the
# forest key), the dark forest (the wolves, the hermit's riddle and the hollow oak's seal, the old bear, the shrine), the
# lake (the drowned chapel, the pike, the third seal), the castle (the portcullis, the kitchens' rats, the crown vault,
# the Beast, the throne room) and the coronation.
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe last_kingdom) through the editor's own operations.
include lib_rt
include lib_huts
include lib_relay
include lib_selene
include lib_sea
new
# (nature: forest, Like Raft's Balboa - birch and pine outside the town, the fields and the castle; the dark forest denser)
gen Trees=0.21 Bushes=0.38 Rocks=0.42 Harvest=0.1 BeachThings=0.3
gen Seed=9226 Radius=200 Height=60 Roughness=0.4 Peaks=2 Shape=7 Style=3 BeachWidth=0.45 Cliffs=0.3 PeakShape=0.45 Lakes=0.4 Valleys=0.5
gen Water=0.5 SeaRocks=0.3 SeaFinds=0.3 Sunken=0.4 Hostiles=0 Friendly=0 SeaLife=0
generate

# ===== THE LAND ===========================================================================================================
# The kingdom (the map, seed 9226): two peaks - the northern one (53 m at 30 60) under the dark forest, the southern one
# (57 m at -20 -70) with the castle on its shoulder (-33 -50, 40 m) - a low valley between them on the west, lowland all
# along the north coast. The lake dug in the valley (-75 5, 9 m down in its middle); the river from the lake north through
# the lowland to the sea (-75 25 > -70 70 > -57 95 > -45 120 > -25 145 > -20 182, 2 m under the sea's level, a ford at
# -42 125); the harbour town on the north coast east of the river's mouth (2 m, x -12..36, z 145..178); the toll bridge
# over the river at -22 150; the mill (west bank, -67 100), the barley fields (-78 125) and the farm (-60 145) west of the
# river; the forest gate at -20 110 (the palisade along the forest's edge); the woodcutter -8 106, the wolves' clearing
# 2 98, the hermit 14 80, the glade of oaks 26 98, the shrine on the forest's south edge -30 45; the ferry landing on the
# lake's east shore -55 12, the castle road's foot -63 -14, its four legs up to the castle's west gate (-46 -50).

# --- Terrain: the town and its quay; the mill's yard, the fields, the farm; the forest's clearings; the shrine's knoll; the
# lake (a wide bowl, a deep middle); the castle's court, the vault's pit, the castle road; then the river cut through it
# all (and its ford) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
