# --- Raft's finds in the shallows round the kingdom (lib_sea; keep this after the terrain and building lines) -----------
call shallows r=220 deep=5 n=3

# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (40 steps, 6 chapters) =============================================
info title=The Last Kingdom
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A whole small kingdom on one island - a harbour town, farmland and a mill along a river, a dark forest, a lake with a drowned chapel and a castle on the hill - empty until its crown is found. Gather the three royal seals across the kingdom, open the crown vault, face the Beast in the great hall and crown the empty throne.
island on.arrive=message||A kingdom: a harbour town with flags on its roofs, fields and a mill along a river, a dark forest over the northern peak - and on the southern one's shoulder, a castle. No smoke from any chimney, no one on the quay.

story writ|Reeve's writ|quest:Tangaroa_Tape|The town reeve's writ, sealed in red: LET THE BEARER PASS THE TOLL.
story seal|Royal seal|quest:Tangaroa_Token|One of the three royal seals of Elderhaven, a stag in gold on black stone.
story forestkey|Forest gate key|quest:Caravan_KeyInfirmary|The key to the palisade gate of the dark forest.
story crown|The crown of Elderhaven|Hat_Mayor|A plain gold crown with a stag on its brow.
story royalseal|The royal charter|Placeable_PaperBundle|The royal charter of Elderhaven, made out in your name.

note proclamation The herald's proclamation | HEAR YE - THE PEOPLE OF ELDERHAVEN\n\nKing Aldric is dead and has left no heir. His steward has hidden the crown and fled. We go to the mainland until the throne is filled.\n\nWhoever brings the crown out of its hiding and sets it on the empty throne may call this kingdom theirs. We will come home to them.\n\nThe reeve's writ for the toll bridge is in the guildhall.\n- the Herald
note poulterer Poulterer's crate | The poulterer's crate on the market: feed, egg boxes - and the net launcher she used on runaway hens.
loot poulterer NetGun*1;NetCanister*8;Egg*2
prop poulterer loot.refill=0
note guildhall Guildhall chest | The guildhall's chest: the town's ledgers, wax, and the reeve's writ for the toll bridge.
loot guildhall story:writ*1;Rope*3;TradeToken*3
prop guildhall loot.refill=0
note innchest Innkeeper's thanks | The innkeeper's thanks for catching her hens: a hot pie, ale - and a word: "The steward hid three seals. One went into the mill's hopper, I saw him. One into the dark forest. One into the lake, where the old chapel drowned."
loot innchest Cooked_GenericMeat*3;PlasticBottle_Water*2;Raw_Potato*2
prop innchest loot.refill=0
prop innchest if.open=quest|5
prop innchest else.open=message||The innkeeper's chest, padlocked. A chalked note: WHOEVER CATCHES MY HENS GETS A PIE.
note millerledger The miller's ledger | THE MILL - LEDGER\n\nThe steward came at night and dropped something heavy into the hopper - I heard it ring on the stones. The mill race was shut at the time; open the sluice and the wheel turns and the hopper empties. Lever by the race.\n\nAlso: the boars are in the barley again, and the farmer's goats are out.
note farmchest Farmer's chest | The farmer's chest: a goat bell, a wedge of cheese - and the key to the forest gate, which only the farm keeps.
loot farmchest story:forestkey*1;Cooked_GenericMeat*2
prop farmchest loot.refill=0
prop farmchest if.open=quest|12
prop farmchest else.open=message||The farmer's chest. A tag: FOR WHOEVER BRINGS MY GOATS IN.
note woodcutter The woodcutter's warning | (nailed to the hut's door)\n\nWOLVES in the clearing past the hut. The OLD BEAR at the glade of the four oaks. The hermit in the deepest wood knows where the steward went - he saw him dig.\nCut what wood you like. Mind your back.
note riddle The hermit's riddle | (carved on a board by the hermit's door)\n\nFour oaks in the glade, all hollow.\nThe fox's oak, the stag's oak, the bee's oak lie.\nWhere the owl keeps watch at night, the seal sleeps.\nReach in.
note ferrychart The ferryman's chart | THE LAKE - FERRYMAN'S CHART\n\nThe old chapel drowned when the dam broke: nine metres, in the lake's middle - you can see its spire at low water. Air under its roof, two pockets.\nTHE PIKE. Big as a boat. Lives round the chapel. I don't swim there.
note reliquary The chapel's reliquary | The reliquary on the drowned altar: a saint's bone in silver - and the third royal seal.
loot reliquary story:seal*1;TradeToken*2
prop reliquary loot.refill=0
note confession The steward's confession | (left on the castle well's rim, under a stone)\n\nI hid the crown in the vault under the castle court and locked it with the three seals. I scattered them. I was afraid of whoever would want it.\nThe Beast came into the great hall the night the king died. It sleeps until somebody takes the crown. Then it wakes.\nForgive me.\n- Osric, steward
note crownchest The crown's chest | In the vault, on velvet: the crown of Elderhaven, plain gold, a stag on its brow.
loot crownchest story:crown*1;CopperIngot*2
prop crownchest loot.refill=0
prop crownchest on.open=show|beast\nshow|beastmusic\nmessage||Above you, in the great hall, something huge wakes - and roars.\nsound||event:/wildlife/bear/bear_roar
note will King Aldric's will | (on the throne's arm)\n\nI leave no heir. I leave a kingdom.\nWhoever sets the crown on this throne after me: be kinder to it than I was. Open the treasury for the people's sake - and call them home.\n- Aldric
note charter The royal charter | THE ROYAL CHARTER OF ELDERHAVEN\n\nBy the crown set on the empty throne, the kingdom of Elderhaven - its harbour, its fields, its forest, its lake and its castle - is given into the keeping of the one who found the crown.\n\nThe people will come home.
note treasury The royal treasury | The royal treasury: Aldric's gold, titanium from the old mines, the plans for the kingdom's great planting beds, a king's sword, and the old king's coat.
loot treasury TradeToken*25;TitaniumIngot*6;Blueprint_Cropplot_Large_Tier3*1;Sword_Titanium*1;Equipment_LeatherChest*1;MetalIngot*6
prop treasury loot.refill=0
prop treasury if.open=signal|crowned
prop treasury else.open=message||The royal treasury opens for the crowned.
note peoplesgift The people's gift | At the market cross, a chest that wasn't there before, with a ribbon in the kingdom's colours: the people's welcome for their new keeper - seeds of every field, the reeve's spare coin, a captain's hat for the harbour, and the plans for the fishermen's head lamps.
loot peoplesgift Seed_Watermelon*4;Seed_Pineapple*4;Seed_Birch*4;TradeToken*10;Hat_Captain*1;Blueprint_HeadLight*1
prop peoplesgift loot.refill=0
prop peoplesgift obj.name=peoplesgift
prop peoplesgift beh.hidden=1
loot warehousebarrel Plank*6;Nail*10;Rope*2
prop warehousebarrel loot.refill=0
note woodbox Woodpile box | A box by the woodcutter's pile: wedges, rope, a flask.
loot woodbox Rope*3;PlasticBottle_Water*1;Plank*4
prop woodbox loot.refill=0
note shrinebox Forest shrine box | Offerings at the forest shrine: candles, coins, dried berries.
loot shrinebox TradeToken*2;Berries_Red*4;Stone*2
prop shrinebox loot.refill=0
note pantrybox Castle pantry box | The castle pantry's box, gnawed: tins the rats couldn't open.
loot pantrybox Cooked_GenericMeat*3;Raw_Potato*3
prop pantrybox loot.refill=0
note quaycrate Sunk crate | A crate that fell off the quay: iron and nails.
loot quaycrate MetalOre*3;Nail*8;Scrap*2
prop quaycrate loot.refill=0
note fordbox Box at the ford | A box at the river's ford: a fisher's tackle.
loot fordbox FishingBait_Simple*3;Rope*2;Cooked_Herring*1
prop fordbox loot.refill=0
note lakebarrel Sunk barrel in the lake | A barrel on the lake's floor from the drowned village.
loot lakebarrel Clay*3;CopperOre*2;Scrap*2
prop lakebarrel loot.refill=0

